      "writtenOn": "2026-05-01T08:20:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree this is delicate and weird. The problem is that hyp_page_count() is used on pages not from page_alloc, hence won\u0027t have the extra ref, and also these pages can validly have a zero refcount. I\u0027m looking at __pkvm_host_unshare_hyp() and __pkvm_guest_relinquish_to_host() for example.\n\nHence I think we need to leave hyp_page_count() alone, but I\u0027m not greatly in love with hyp_pagetable_count() and we could: Rename it; and/or Move it; and/or Make its return value essentially a boolean-in-an-int as you suggest.",
      "parentUuid": "016c18fc_20b8757d",
